IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23), s 2: the definitions that can be worked out from facts,
-- and the interpretation rules of s 2(2). Written by the keel agent (ei-g0).
-- Text: the unofficial plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws consolidation current to 2026-09-30.
-- Seat: the person who has lost work or cannot work and asks whether they qualify for benefits.
--
-- Every rule below takes plain facts as its own GIVEN parameters, named in the Act's own words, because
-- the stable binary rejects a GIVEN placed on a section. A definition whose meaning is decided in another
-- piece's range is NOT encoded here: NOTES.md "Defined terms" says which piece encodes it and what plain
-- input every other piece should take for it.

§ `The Parts of the Act`

-- A definition below keys on the Part of the Act a benefit is payable under (s 2(1) "benefits",
-- "regular benefits", "Minister"). The heading of each Part is its source.
-- src:133 | PART I Unemployment Benefits
-- src:1049 | PART II Employment Support Measures and National Employment Service
-- src:1127 | PART III Premiums and Other Financial Matters
-- src:1294 | PART IV Insurable Earnings and Collection of Premiums
-- src:1789 | PART V Pilot Projects
-- src:1804 | PART VI Administrative Provisions
-- src:2054 | PART VII Benefit Repayment
-- src:2109 | PART VII.1 Benefits For Self-Employed Persons
-- src:2689 | PART VIII Self-employed Persons Engaged in Fishing
-- src:2711 | PART VIII.1 Alternate Access to Special Benefits
-- src:2721 | PART VIII.2 Regulations — Provincial Plans
-- src:2735 | PART VIII.3 Interim Orders
-- src:2763 | PART VIII.4 Employment Insurance Emergency Response Benefit
-- src:2967 | PART VIII.5 Temporary Measures to Facilitate Access to Benefits
-- src:3086 | PART VIII.6 Temporary Measures
-- src:3096 | PART IX Repeals, Transitional Provisions, Related and Conditional Amendments and Coming into Force
@ref Employment Insurance Act Parts I to IX (src:133) (src:1049) (src:1127) (src:1294) (src:1789) (src:1804) (src:2054) (src:2109) (src:2689) (src:2711) (src:2721) (src:2735) (src:2763) (src:2967) (src:3086) (src:3096)
DECLARE `Part of the Act` IS ONE OF
    `Part I`
    `Part II`
    `Part III`
    `Part IV`
    `Part V`
    `Part VI`
    `Part VII`
    `Part VII.1`
    `Part VIII`
    `Part VIII.1`
    `Part VIII.2`
    `Part VIII.3`
    `Part VIII.4`
    `Part VIII.5`
    `Part VIII.6`
    `Part IX`

§ `Section 2(1) - definitions worked out from facts`

-- src:18 | affidavit means an affidavit sworn or affirmed before a commissioner of oaths or any other person authorized to take affidavits; (affidavit)
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 2(1) "affidavit" (src:18)
GIVEN `sworn or affirmed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `before a commissioner of oaths` IS A BOOLEAN
      `before any other person authorized to take affidavits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 2(1) affidavit` IF
        `sworn or affirmed`
    AND (`before a commissioner of oaths` OR `before any other person authorized to take affidavits`)

-- src:20 | benefits means unemployment benefits payable under Part I, VII.1 or VIII; (prestation)
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 2(1) "benefits" (src:20)
GIVEN `the Part under which the unemployment benefits are payable` IS A `Part of the Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 2(1) benefits` IF
       `the Part under which the unemployment benefits are payable` EQUALS `Part I`
    OR `the Part under which the unemployment benefits are payable` EQUALS `Part VII.1`
    OR `the Part under which the unemployment benefits are payable` EQUALS `Part VIII`

-- src:22 | claimant means a person who applies or has applied for benefits under this Act; (prestataire)
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 2(1) "claimant" (src:22)
GIVEN `applies for benefits under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `has applied for benefits under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 2(1) claimant` IF
       `applies for benefits under this Act`
    OR `has applied for benefits under this Act`

-- src:24 | common-law partner, in relation to an individual, means a person who is cohabiting with the individual in a conjugal relationship, having so cohabited for a period of at least one year; (conjoint de fait)
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 2(1) "common-law partner" (src:24)
GIVEN `cohabiting with the individual in a conjugal relationship` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the first day of their cohabitation` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 2(1) common-law partner` IF
        `cohabiting with the individual in a conjugal relationship`
    AND (`add years` `the first day of their cohabitation` 1) AT MOST `the day on which the question is asked`

-- src:25 | confirmed delivery service means certified or registered mail or any other delivery service that provides proof of delivery; (service de messagerie)
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 2(1) "confirmed delivery service" (src:25)
GIVEN `certified mail` IS A BOOLEAN
      `registered mail` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any other delivery service that provides proof of delivery` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 2(1) confirmed delivery service` IF
       `certified mail`
    OR `registered mail`
    OR `any other delivery service that provides proof of delivery`

-- "documents includes ..." is an open list: the Act does not say what else a document is. So the rule
-- answers JUST TRUE for a listed kind and NOTHING for anything else, and never FALSE.
-- src:26 | documents includes money, securities, books, records, letters, telegrams, vouchers, invoices, accounts and statements (financial or otherwise); (documents)
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 2(1) "documents" (src:26)
DECLARE `Kind of thing the definition of documents lists` IS ONE OF
    `s 2(1) documents - money`
    `s 2(1) documents - securities`
    `s 2(1) documents - books`
    `s 2(1) documents - records`
    `s 2(1) documents - letters`
    `s 2(1) documents - telegrams`
    `s 2(1) documents - vouchers`
    `s 2(1) documents - invoices`
    `s 2(1) documents - accounts`
    `s 2(1) documents - statements, financial or otherwise`
    `s 2(1) documents - something not on the list`

-- src:26 | documents includes money, securities, books, records, letters, telegrams, vouchers, invoices, accounts and statements (financial or otherwise); (documents)
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 2(1) "documents" (src:26)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of thing the definition of documents lists`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 2(1) documents includes` IS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 2(1) documents - something not on the list` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:27 | dwelling-house means the whole or any part of a building or structure that is kept or occupied as a permanent or temporary residence and includes
-- src:28 | (a) a building within the yard of a dwelling-house that is connected to it by a doorway or by a covered and enclosed passageway, and
-- src:29 | (b) a unit that is designed to be mobile and to be used as a permanent or temporary residence and that is being used as a residence; (maison d’habitation)
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 2(1) "dwelling-house" (src:27-29)
GIVEN `the whole or any part of a building or structure that is kept or occupied as a permanent or temporary residence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a building within the yard of a dwelling-house` IS A BOOLEAN
      `connected to it by a doorway` IS A BOOLEAN
      `connected to it by a covered and enclosed passageway` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a unit that is designed to be mobile and to be used as a permanent or temporary residence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that unit is being used as a residence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 2(1) dwelling-house` IF
       `the whole or any part of a building or structure that is kept or occupied as a permanent or temporary residence`
    OR (`a building within the yard of a dwelling-house` AND (`connected to it by a doorway` OR `connected to it by a covered and enclosed passageway`))
    OR (`a unit that is designed to be mobile and to be used as a permanent or temporary residence` AND `that unit is being used as a residence`)

-- src:31 | employer includes a person who has been an employer and, in respect of remuneration of an individual referred to as sponsor or co-ordinator of a project in paragraph 5(1)(e), it includes that individual; (employeur)
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 2(1) "employer" (src:31)
GIVEN `is an employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `has been an employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is the individual referred to as sponsor or co-ordinator of a project in paragraph 5(1)(e)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the question concerns the remuneration of that individual` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 2(1) employer` IF
       `is an employer`
    OR `has been an employer`
    OR (`is the individual referred to as sponsor or co-ordinator of a project in paragraph 5(1)(e)` AND `the question concerns the remuneration of that individual`)

-- src:33 | employment means the act of employing or the state of being employed; (emploi)
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 2(1) "employment" (src:33)
GIVEN `the act of employing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the state of being employed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 2(1) employment` IF
       `the act of employing`
    OR `the state of being employed`

-- src:38 | insured person means a person who is or has been employed in insurable employment; (assuré)
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 2(1) "insured person" (src:38)
GIVEN `is employed in insurable employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `has been employed in insurable employment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 2(1) insured person` IF
       `is employed in insurable employment`
    OR `has been employed in insurable employment`

-- src:40 | labour dispute means a dispute between employers and employees, or between employees and employees, that is connected with the employment or non-employment, or the terms or conditions of employment, of any persons; (conflit collectif)
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 2(1) "labour dispute" (src:40)
GIVEN `a dispute between employers and employees` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a dispute between employees and employees` IS A BOOLEAN
      `connected with the employment of any persons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `connected with the non-employment of any persons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `connected with the terms or conditions of employment of any persons` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 2(1) labour dispute` IF
        (`a dispute between employers and employees` OR `a dispute between employees and employees`)
    AND (`connected with the employment of any persons` OR `connected with the non-employment of any persons` OR `connected with the terms or conditions of employment of any persons`)

-- The Minister is the Minister of National Revenue in Parts IV and VII, because s 81 and s 144 say so
-- for their own Parts; everywhere else it is the Minister of Employment and Social Development.
-- src:42 | Minister means the Minister of Employment and Social Development, except in Parts IV and VII; (ministre)
-- src:1301 | Minister means the Minister of National Revenue. (ministre)
-- src:2063 | Minister means the Minister of National Revenue; (ministre)
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 2(1) "Minister" (src:42); s 81 "Minister" (src:1301); s 144 "Minister" (src:2063)
GIVEN part IS A `Part of the Act`
GIVETH A Party
DECIDE `s 2(1) the Minister for` IS
    CONSIDER part
    WHEN `Part IV` THEN `the Minister of National Revenue`
    WHEN `Part VII` THEN `the Minister of National Revenue`
    OTHERWISE `the Minister`

-- The positive meaning of "overpayment of benefits" is given in Part VI (piece ei4); only the
-- exclusion belongs to s 2(1), so the positive meaning is a plain input here.
-- src:43 | overpayment of benefits does not include a benefit repayment as described in Part VII; (versement excédentaire de prestations)
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 2(1) "overpayment of benefits" (src:43)
GIVEN `is an overpayment of benefits apart from this exclusion` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is a benefit repayment as described in Part VII` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 2(1) overpayment of benefits` IF
        `is an overpayment of benefits apart from this exclusion`
    AND NOT (`is a benefit repayment as described in Part VII`)

-- src:45 | provincial law means the provisions of any Act of the legislature of a province authorizing, or entitling a person to, the payment of benefits under a plan established by or under that Act; (loi provinciale)
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 2(1) "provincial law" (src:45)
GIVEN `the provisions of an Act of the legislature of a province` IS A BOOLEAN
      `authorizing the payment of benefits under a plan established by or under that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `entitling a person to the payment of benefits under a plan established by or under that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 2(1) provincial law` IF
        `the provisions of an Act of the legislature of a province`
    AND (`authorizing the payment of benefits under a plan established by or under that Act` OR `entitling a person to the payment of benefits under a plan established by or under that Act`)

-- "special benefits" is worked out first because "regular benefits" excludes it.
-- src:48 | special benefits means benefits paid for any reason mentioned in subsection 12(3) or 152.14(1); (prestations spéciales)
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 2(1) "special benefits" (src:48)
GIVEN reason IS A `Reason for benefits`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 2(1) special benefits` IF
    NOT (reason EQUALS `a reason other than those mentioned in subsection 12(3)`)

-- src:47 | regular benefits means benefits payable under Part I and Part VIII, but does not include special benefits or benefits by virtue of section 24 or 25; (prestations régulières)
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 2(1) "regular benefits" (src:47)
GIVEN `the Part under which the benefits are payable` IS A `Part of the Act`
      `they are special benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are paid by virtue of section 24 or 25` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 2(1) regular benefits` IF
        (`the Part under which the benefits are payable` EQUALS `Part I` OR `the Part under which the benefits are payable` EQUALS `Part VIII`)
    AND NOT (`they are special benefits`)
    AND NOT (`they are paid by virtue of section 24 or 25`)

-- src:50 | week means a period of seven consecutive days beginning on and including Sunday, or any other prescribed period; (semaine)
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 2(1) "week" (src:50)
GIVEN p IS A `Period of days`
      `it is some other prescribed period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 2(1) week` IF
        (`the number of days in` p EQUALS 7 AND `s 2(1) the Sunday that begins the week containing` (p's `first day of the period`) EQUALS p's `first day of the period`)
    OR `it is some other prescribed period`

§ `Section 2(2) - rates of unemployment produced by Statistics Canada`

-- src:53 | (2) If the use of rates of unemployment produced by Statistics Canada is required under this Act or the regulations, the Commission shall use those most recently produced at the time it is appropriate or necessary for the Commission to make a final determination in respect of those rates or involving their use.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 2(2) (src:53)
DECLARE `Published rate of unemployment` HAS
    `date produced` IS A DATE
    `rate produced` IS A NUMBER

-- The Commission uses the rates "most recently produced at the time" it makes its final determination.
-- Assumed, not ruled: a rate produced ON the day of the final determination was produced "at the time".
-- The list a caller passes is the releases for the one region concerned; which region applies to a
-- person is decided by the Regulations (reg 17, piece er1), not here.
-- src:53 | (2) If the use of rates of unemployment produced by Statistics Canada is required under this Act or the regulations, the Commission shall use those most recently produced at the time it is appropriate or necessary for the Commission to make a final determination in respect of those rates or involving their use.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 2(2) (src:53)
GIVEN releases IS A LIST OF `Published rate of unemployment`
      `the day of the final determination` IS A DATE
GIVETH A LIST OF `Published rate of unemployment`
DECIDE `s 2(2) the rates produced by` IS
    filter (GIVEN r YIELD r's `date produced` AT MOST `the day of the final determination`) releases

-- src:53 | (2) If the use of rates of unemployment produced by Statistics Canada is required under this Act or the regulations, the Commission shall use those most recently produced at the time it is appropriate or necessary for the Commission to make a final determination in respect of those rates or involving their use.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 2(2) (src:53)
GIVEN eligible IS A LIST OF `Published rate of unemployment`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 2(2) the latest day of production among` IS
    maximum (map (GIVEN q YIELD Day (q's `date produced`)) eligible)

-- src:53 | (2) If the use of rates of unemployment produced by Statistics Canada is required under this Act or the regulations, the Commission shall use those most recently produced at the time it is appropriate or necessary for the Commission to make a final determination in respect of those rates or involving their use.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 2(2) (src:53)
GIVEN eligible IS A LIST OF `Published rate of unemployment`
      latest IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF `Published rate of unemployment`
DECIDE `s 2(2) the releases produced on the day numbered` IS
    filter (GIVEN r YIELD Day (r's `date produced`) EQUALS latest) eligible

-- src:53 | (2) If the use of rates of unemployment produced by Statistics Canada is required under this Act or the regulations, the Commission shall use those most recently produced at the time it is appropriate or necessary for the Commission to make a final determination in respect of those rates or involving their use.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 2(2) (src:53)
GIVEN release IS A `Published rate of unemployment`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 2(2) the rate in` IS release's `rate produced`

-- src:53 | (2) If the use of rates of unemployment produced by Statistics Canada is required under this Act or the regulations, the Commission shall use those most recently produced at the time it is appropriate or necessary for the Commission to make a final determination in respect of those rates or involving their use.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 2(2) (src:53)
GIVEN releases IS A LIST OF `Published rate of unemployment`
      `the day of the final determination` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 2(2) the rate of unemployment most recently produced` IS
    IF null (`s 2(2) the rates produced by` releases `the day of the final determination`)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`s 2(2) the rate in` (at (`s 2(2) the releases produced on the day numbered` (`s 2(2) the rates produced by` releases `the day of the final determination`) (`s 2(2) the latest day of production among` (`s 2(2) the rates produced by` releases `the day of the final determination`))) 0))
